<!--
  <sui-error-state> — SUI port of <ship-error-state>.
  Sibling of <sui-empty-state> for "something broke" paths.
  Destructive tone halo, collapsible technical details, auto-focused retry.

  Prop parity vs <ship-error-state>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  title (string, '')           title (string, '')       ✓ fallback in template
  body (string, '')            body (string, '')        ✓
  size ('sm'|'md'|'lg', 'md') size (sm|md|lg, 'md',    ✓
                                 reflect)
  variant ('default'|'inline') variant (default|inline, ✓
                                 'default', reflect)
  icon (string, 'alert-circle') icon (string,           ✓ rendered via sui-icon
                                  'alert-circle')
  code (string, '', reflect)   code (string, '',        ✓ (undocumented in the
                                 reflect)                  feat/next table but
                                                           present in its markup)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Details toggle visibility    controller sets          ✓ data-has-details on
    driven by slot content       data-has-details         host; CSS targets it
  Details open/close           controller sets          ✓ data-details-open on
                                 data-details-open        host; CSS targets it
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  slots: title, (default),     title, (default),        ✓
         details, action         details, action
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  parts: box, icon, title,     box, icon, title,        ✓ (feat/next's own
         desc, actions           desc, actions, code,      markup also carries
                                  details-toggle            part=code/details-
                                                            toggle despite the
                                                            table above omitting
                                                            them — kept, the
                                                            test file selects
                                                            on them)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  role="alert" on box div      same                     ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone prop exists on this component at all — it's ALWAYS the destructive
    halo (that's the point of an error state). The worktree's prior spike
    invented a fake "tone" theme channel with a single "default" case for a
    prop that doesn't exist; dropped. `.icon`/`.box` read the destructive
    tokens (var(--destructive), var(--tone-destructive-bg), etc.) directly,
    unconditionally — no theme block, no variant needed for it.
  - Controller is BYTE-IDENTICAL to feat/next.
  - The details-toggle is now a bare framework `<button ghost xs>` instead of
    a hand-rolled CSS reset (appearance:none / background:transparent /
    border:0 / padding / border-radius / hover color+bg). The xs size channel
    supplies --size-fs:text-xs for free (an exact match for feat/next's
    text-xs toggle label). Per the alert pilot's precedented deviation, the
    custom hover (color:foreground, bg:muted) is dropped in favor of the
    ghost skin's own hover treatment.
  - `weight:semibold` used directly instead of consuming the `--heading-
    weight` alias — same numeric value (`--heading-weight` IS `--font-weight-
    semibold`), now spelled through the sx-native token.
  - sx is closed-vocabulary; `<style>` keeps only what sx structurally cannot
    express: `.box`/`.icon`'s flex setup (display/flex-direction/align-items/
    justify-content/flex-shrink — none of these are sx props, matching how
    sui-alert kept its own `.box`/`.ico` flex setup fully in style), `gap`,
    `text-align` (no sx prop for it at all), `.actions`'s `display:flex` (sx's
    Display enum only has "inline-flex", not plain "flex" — see LANG-GAP),
    `appearance`, `font-family` (heading/mono), `white-space`/`word-break`,
    the `:empty` pseudo-class, the icon's inset ring box-shadow (a shape
    `ring:` can't produce — that channel only emits the framework's 2-layer
    OUTER glow, never a single inset line), and the forced-colors query.
  - Sizes (sm/md/lg): pad-x, gap, title/desc font sizes, and the inline-
    variant's own icon size (22/16/28px) all land EXACTLY on existing tokens
    (space-4/6, space-2/3/4, text-base/md/lg, control-h-2xs/icon-size-md/
    icon-size-3xl). Two dimensions do not: the default-variant icon TILE
    (48/36/64px for md/sm/lg) and the box's vertical padding (64/32/96px).
    sm lands exactly (space-9=36, space-7=32); md/lg do not — see LANG-GAP.
  - LANG-GAP: the space/control-h token scales top out at space-8 (40px) /
    control-h-xl (44px). feat/next's lg-size hero padding (96px) and icon
    tile (64px) are far past that ceiling — not a "nearest token is a few px
    off" rounding, an actual missing tier. md's targets (64px pad-y, 48px
    tile) also exceed the ceiling, landing on the SAME maxed-out tokens
    (space-8, control-h-xl) that lg is forced to. Net effect: the md and lg
    sizes' outer padding and icon-tile dimensions are now IDENTICAL where
    feat/next scaled them apart — only gap/text still differentiate md vs
    lg. Reported per the LANG-GAP protocol; the fix is a language/token-
    registry addition (a hero-scale space step past space-8, and a control-h
    step past control-h-xl), not something this file can route around.
  - max-width: 40ch/60ch (desc/details) both land within 2ch of existing
    panel-ch-w-md (38ch) / panel-ch-w-lg (60ch, exact) tokens — the same
    quantization already precedented for sui-toast's panel-w snapping.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    title: '',
    body: '',
    size: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg',
    variant: 'default' | 'inline',
    icon: 'alert-circle',
  },
}</component>

<prop name="code" type="string" default="" reflect />

<variants class="box">
  [variant='inline']: radius:md shadow:none py:3 px:4 bg:tone-destructive-bg border:tone-destructive-border
  size=sm: py:7
  size=lg: py:8 px:6
</variants>

<variants class="icon">
  size=sm: w:9 h:9
  size=lg: w:control-h-xl h:control-h-xl
  [variant='inline']: bg:tone-destructive-bg w:control-h-2xs h:control-h-2xs leading:none
  (variant=inline, size=sm): w:icon-size-md h:icon-size-md
  (variant=inline, size=lg): w:icon-size-3xl h:icon-size-3xl
</variants>

<variants class="title">
  size=sm: text:base
  size=lg: text:lg
</variants>

<variants class="desc">
  size=lg: text:base
</variants>

<variants class="details-toggle">
  [data-has-details]: display:inline-block
</variants>

<variants class="details">
  ([data-has-details], [data-details-open]): display:block
</variants>

<style>
  :host {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }
  :host([hidden]) { display: none; }

  .box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    text-align: center;
  }
  :host([size='sm']) .box { gap: var(--space-2); }
  :host([size='lg']) .box { gap: var(--space-4); }
  :host([variant='inline']) .box {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    text-align: start;
  }

  .icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--tone-destructive-ring);
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) .icon { box-shadow: none; }

  .title { font-family: var(--heading-font); }

  .code:empty { display: none; }

  .details {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
    text-align: start;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) .actions {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .box { border-color: CanvasText; }
    .icon { background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; }
  }
</style>


<controller>
import { controller, effect } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import type { Scope } from './sui-error-state.sui'

export default controller<Scope>({
  mount(state, host) {
    let detailsOpen = false

    const updateToggleLabel = (btn: HTMLButtonElement) => {
      btn.textContent = detailsOpen ? 'Hide details' : 'Show details'
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', detailsOpen ? 'true' : 'false')
    }

    const stopDetailsSlot = effect(() => {
      const slot = state.$signals.detailsSlot() as HTMLSlotElement | null
      if (!slot) return
      const check = () => {
        const hasContent = slot.assignedNodes({ flatten: true }).some(n =>
          n.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE ||
          (n.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE && (n.textContent ?? '').trim().length > 0),
        )
        if (hasContent) {
          host.setAttribute('data-has-details', '')
        } else {
          host.removeAttribute('data-has-details')
          host.removeAttribute('data-details-open')
          detailsOpen = false
          const btn = state.$signals.detailsToggleBtn() as HTMLButtonElement | null
          if (btn) updateToggleLabel(btn)
        }
      }
      slot.addEventListener('slotchange', check)
      check()
      return () => slot.removeEventListener('slotchange', check)
    })

    const stopToggleInit = effect(() => {
      const btn = state.$signals.detailsToggleBtn() as HTMLButtonElement | null
      if (!btn) return
      updateToggleLabel(btn)
      const onClick = () => {
        detailsOpen = !detailsOpen
        if (detailsOpen) {
          host.setAttribute('data-details-open', '')
        } else {
          host.removeAttribute('data-details-open')
        }
        updateToggleLabel(btn)
      }
      btn.addEventListener('click', onClick)
      return () => btn.removeEventListener('click', onClick)
    })

    const stopActionSlot = effect(() => {
      const slot = state.$signals.actionSlot() as HTMLSlotElement | null
      if (!slot) return
      const onSlotChange = () => {
        const retry = slot.assignedElements().find(
          el => el.getAttribute('slot') === 'retry',
        ) as HTMLElement | undefined
        if (retry) requestAnimationFrame(() => retry.focus?.())
      }
      slot.addEventListener('slotchange', onSlotChange)
      return () => slot.removeEventListener('slotchange', onSlotChange)
    })

    return () => {
      stopDetailsSlot()
      stopToggleInit()
      stopActionSlot()
    }
  },
})

</controller>
<div class="box" part="box" role="alert"
  sx="py:8 px:4 radius:lg shadow:xs bg:tone-muted-bg border:border">
  <div class="icon" part="icon" aria-hidden="true"
    sx="w:control-h-xl h:control-h-xl radius:lg bg:tone-destructive-bg fg:destructive leading:none">
    <sui-icon name={icon()} size="md"></sui-icon>
  </div>

  <column class="copy" gap="1" align={variant() === 'inline' ? 'start' : 'center'} sx="min-w:0">
    <div class="title" part="title" sx="text:md weight:semibold fg:foreground leading:tight">
      <slot name="title">{title() || 'Something went wrong'}</slot>
    </div>
    <div class="desc" part="desc" sx="text:sm max-w:panel-ch-w-md leading:normal-plus fg:muted-foreground">
      <slot>{body()}</slot>
    </div>
    <div class="code" part="code" sx="text:xs fg:muted-foreground bg:muted border:subtle radius:sm py:1 px:2 mt:1">{code()}</div>
    <button ghost xs class="details-toggle" part="details-toggle" bind:this={detailsToggleBtn} type="button" sx="display:none mt:1"></button>
    <div class="details" part="details" bind:this={detailsPanel}
      sx="display:none mt:2 py:2 px:3 bg:tone-destructive-bg radius:sm text:xs fg:muted-foreground max-w:panel-ch-w-lg">
      <slot name="details" bind:this={detailsSlot}></slot>
    </div>
  </column>

  <div class="actions" part="actions" sx="mt:1">
    <slot name="action" bind:this={actionSlot}></slot>
  </div>
</div>
